      role1: "CEO & Artistic Director",
      bio1: "A Swiss director, writer, audiovisual programmer and producer, Dario Cirrincione serves as General Manager and Artistic Director of the Merge Film Festival. He is co-founder of the independent company PoPaCi Pictures SNC, through which he develops film and art projects as well as cultural initiatives in Switzerland and internationally. He directed Present, a short film that explores and blends various expressive formats, including the use of artificial intelligence. The film has been selected for several international festivals, including the World AI Film Festival.",
      role2: "COO & Artistic Director",
      bio2: "A Swiss director, writer, audiovisual programmer and producer, Francesco Poloni serves as Chief Operating Officer and Artistic Director of the Merge Film Festival. He is co-founder of the independent company PoPaCi Pictures SNC, through which he develops film and art projects and cultural initiatives between Switzerland and the international scene. He directed the short film Tusen Toner, which was selected for the Pardi di domani section of the 2025 Locarno Film Festival, where it won the SRG SSR Silver Pardino, one of the leading awards dedicated to emerging filmmakers.",
      role4: "CTO, Creative Technologist",
      bio4: "Born in Lugano in 2003, Thomas Zaffalon serves as CTO and Creative Technologist of the Merge Film Festival. After studying at CISA, where he earned a diploma in Visual Design in 2024 alongside Dario and the rest of the team, he continued with a Bachelor of Informatics at USI and spent his third year at Sapienza University of Rome. Today he oversees the Merge Film Festival's digital infrastructure, from internal systems to web platforms, connecting audiovisual sensitivity with software, web architecture and digital operations. He also designed and built this website.",
      role3: "CCO",
      bio3: "Born in Varese in 2002 and raised between Italy and Canton Ticino, Davide Macchi serves as Chief Communications Officer of the Merge Film Festival. His path brings together scientific and artistic studies, and in 2025 he graduated from CISA in Locarno, where editing and post-production became his main creative strength. He edited the graduation short film Tusen Toner, selected for the Pardi di domani section of the 78th Locarno Film Festival, where it won the SRG SSR Silver Pardino. For Merge he leads the festival's communications, shaping its public voice across social channels and beyond while overseeing its brand identity.",
      role5: "Film Selector",
      bio5: "A Swiss editor, filmmaker and audiovisual selector, Martina Agueci serves as film selector for the Merge Film Festival. Active in the field of cinema and the audiovisual arts, she combines editing work with the research and selection of cinematographic works, with particular attention to contemporary languages and new forms of experimentation. Her path develops between creative practice and audiovisual curation, with an interest in the dialogue between cinema, technology and narrative innovation.",
      role6: "Film Selector",
      bio6: "A Ticino actress and theatre performer, Manila Tunesi serves as film selector for the Merge Film Festival. After graduating from Bologna's Alessandra Galante Garrone Academy and taking part in the creation of several film projects, she continues her research toward political, independent and collective theatre. She has collaborated for years with Living Theatre Europa, Teatro Periferico and the theatre group Collettivo Vento. After her academic path, she chose to experiment with contemporary hybrid and performative languages capable of enriching her projects and research.",
      role7: "Film Selector",
      bio7: "Lucas Previtali is a Swiss editor and writer working in film. His work is driven by a long-standing interest in film critique and a growing focus on the aesthetics and language of digital cinema, as well as the exploration of new forms of visual storytelling. He edited the graduation short film For Your Own Good, which premiered at the Locarno Film Festival's school shorts section and was selected for the Fribourg International Film Festival. He serves as a selector of the Merge Film Festival and is currently writing his first film, an animated short.",
